        'It stays the same',
        'It depends on the season',
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'Revenue is price × quantity, and the two move opposite ways when price changes. When demand is inelastic (|PED| below 1), the price effect dominates, so raising price raises revenue — the arithmetic behind "sin taxes" on inelastic goods and why luxury sellers, facing elastic demand, cannot simply price up.',
    },
